<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Biscay</h1><p class="st-meta">1040 CE – 1379 CE (approx.) · capital Bilbao</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Basque lordship ruled by the Haro family under Navarre and Castile, whose fueros and assembly at Guernica made it a byword for local liberties.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1040 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inigo-lopez-ezquerra">Íñigo López Ezquerra</a> appears in records as the first count or lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Biscay</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-haro">López de Haro</a>, held the lordship for more than three centuries, moving their allegiance between Navarre and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lords ruled with the consent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juntas-generales-of-biscay">Juntas Generales</a>, the general assembly that met under the oak of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guernica">Guernica</a> and guarded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Biscay's</a> fueros, or customary laws. The economy depended on iron mining, forges, shipbuilding and fishing. In 1300 Lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-lopez-v-de-haro">Diego López V de Haro</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilbao">Bilbao</a>, which grew into its chief port.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1379 the lordship passed by inheritance to John I of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile</a>, and from then on the kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Biscay</a> as lords. Its fueros survived until the 19th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-biscay.jpg" alt="Lordship of Biscay" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: This vector image includes elements that have been taken or adapted from this file · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https:/